  "title": "Sine Rule, Cosine Rule & Area Formula",
  "content": "<p><strong>Sine Rule:</strong> \\(\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C}\\). Use when you have a side and its opposite angle.</p><p><strong>Cosine Rule (find side):</strong> \\(a^2 = b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos A\\). Use when you have two sides and the included angle (SAS).</p><p><strong>Cosine Rule (find angle):</strong> \\(\\cos A = \\frac{b^2 + c^2 - a^2}{2bc}\\). Use with three sides (SSS).</p><p><strong>Area of triangle:</strong> \\(\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\). Use with two sides and the included angle.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Find side \\(a\\): \\(b = 8\\), \\(c = 10\\), \\(A = 60^\\circ\\).</strong></p><p>\\(a^2 = 64 + 100 - 2(8)(10)\\cos60 = 164 - 80 = 84\\). \\(a = 9.17\\) cm.</p>"
 },
